WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
- So Demi has a podcast called
4D with Demi Lovage and it

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.840
uses this platform to talk
about finding their identity.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.470
So what was that journey like for you?

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.360
Because I feel like when I say "was",

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.130
it's kind of a constant thing, right?

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.930
We're all ever changing, right?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.912
- [Demi] Yes. I like to think
of myself as ever-evolving.

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:20.350
I feel like if you don't change,

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.890
then you're not working on
yourself and I have changed so

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.471
much, I've become so much
more of a spiritual person.

00:00:26.471 --> 00:00:30.616
I started meditating in
quarantine and lockdown.

00:00:30.616 --> 00:00:32.160
- Good on you.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.904
- Well, I think I was just
stoned with nothing to do,

00:00:34.904 --> 00:00:38.413
- (Kelly Laughs) Oh my
God, that's amazing.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:41.390
- But it got me really into meditating.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.030
And so I started meditating
daily and for long periods of

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:49.680
time. And after these intense meditation,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.380
sometimes I would have really
incredible experiences when I

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.100
would open my eyes and look up.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.957
And that's why I talk about
how important meditation is to

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.430
me. But it also brought me on,

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.150
on a personal level that I
was able to go deep inside of

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:08.540
myself and figure out parts
of me that I've never figured

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.889
out before. I came out as
non-binary in April or May.

00:01:12.889 --> 00:01:17.560
And it's been really, really
cool to see so many people,

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:18.980
so supportive of my journey.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.359
I changed my pronouns to "they/them"

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:25.109
- (crowd cheers)

00:01:27.056 --> 00:01:29.870
- And when I try to explain this,

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:33.040
but some people think what
is being non-binary to you?

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.473
For me personally, this
isn't the same for everyone,

00:01:35.473 --> 00:01:40.160
but I feel spiritually balanced
in my masculine and feminine

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.720
energy that I don't particularly
feel more of a woman or a

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.001
man. So I identify as non-binary.

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:49.822
- Wow. It's very bold. It's very cool.

00:01:49.822 --> 00:01:53.830
Well how can someone who
is not sure how to address,

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:54.663
'cause here's the thing, too,

00:01:54.663 --> 00:01:56.440
I always get worried,
because even on The Voice,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.300
like we've had these
conversations with the producers,

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.141
because we're turned around,
and sometimes we, yeah.

00:02:00.141 --> 00:02:03.240
And so we don't know them.
We're not allowed to know them.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.080
So, so it could be, a they,
a she, a he, we don't know.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.300
And so we turn around and
our big thing is like,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.630
God, we don't want to offend anyone.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:13.122
Like, you know, so I think
that's the thing that I,

00:02:13.122 --> 00:02:15.600
I hate the cancel culture and
like, oh, they're canceled.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.620
Cause they said that it's like, no, no,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.740
give them a minute to learn,

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.600
like give them that's the truth, right?

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.310
Like, because it's new for everyone.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.410
So if people feel more
comfortable as they/them

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.140
I'm totally for that. I just think

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.880
you have to allow a little grace, right?

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.880
- [Demi] Yes. You have
to have mercy for people

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.693
that are trying to learn
this new thing. And for me

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:35.430
I still mess up sometimes
because I was born a female and

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:40.130
was female my whole life
until I started identifying as

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.819
non-binary just a few
months ago. So for me,

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:44.528
I even have times where I slip up,

00:02:44.528 --> 00:02:47.250
like someone will be like, yes, girl.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.630
And I'm like, yes.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.366
But like, I don't really,
like you know what I mean?

00:02:50.366 --> 00:02:51.640
It's not really.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.610
- You're like, so.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.270
- I don't take it personally
when someone's like "yes girl".

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.928
I just, I don't know.
I think it's important

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:00.979
that people remember that this is a

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:05.979
new thing and it's absolutely
okay to make an accident as

00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:08.776
long as your intention is right.

00:03:08.776 --> 00:03:11.920
And that's by like, as
long as it's kind of like,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.920
I had an experience with a
friend who had said, you know,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.140
it's kind of like if someone
were to get your name wrong,

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.537
like if someone were to call
you, Carrie, Carrie Clarkston.

00:03:22.537 --> 00:03:24.680
- Well, Carrie Underwood,
they've done it a lot.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.167
- [Demi] Oh no! I was just
like, what sounds like it?

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.887
- I'm like, we look nothing alike at all,

00:03:28.887 --> 00:03:32.380
or but it sounded like,
but I love her, so great.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.440
- Yeah she's great. But it would be like,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.217
if someone continued to call you Carrie,

00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:37.908
even after you correct them and say,

00:03:37.908 --> 00:03:39.627
actually it's Kelly and
they say, okay, Carrie.

00:03:39.627 --> 00:03:42.647
As long as you can understand
how weird it feels,

00:03:42.647 --> 00:03:45.817
when someone messes it
up for another person,

00:03:45.817 --> 00:03:48.530
then you can kind of understand
how the depth and the

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.130
importance of getting it right is,

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.287
and that's all it is about.

00:03:52.287 --> 00:03:53.280
- [Kelly] That's a
great way to explain it.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.220
- Yeah it's just about
accepting each other,

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.708
- Investing, trying. Yeah. Agreed, agreed.

00:03:56.708 --> 00:03:59.577
Well, is it true that you
kind of slid, I love this.

00:03:59.577 --> 00:04:03.537
You slid into the DMS of a
guest you had on your podcast.

00:04:03.537 --> 00:04:04.833
I love this.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:07.723
Is it true?

00:04:07.723 --> 00:04:09.312
- Are we really just
calling me out like that?

00:04:09.312 --> 00:04:12.404
- [Kelly] Yes we just really went there.

00:04:12.404 --> 00:04:14.933
I love that. You really know who you want.

00:04:14.933 --> 00:04:17.740
- I did, I did. Well,
you know, I've always,

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.600
even when I identified as female,

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.505
I was always sliding in the DM's

00:04:21.505 --> 00:04:24.143
like if you don't take your shot,

00:04:24.143 --> 00:04:25.730
how are you going to know
if you're going to get it?

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:26.630
- [Kelly] Exactly.

00:04:27.593 --> 00:04:31.313
So, yeah, I, slid into
Emily Hampshire's DMS

00:04:31.313 --> 00:04:33.044
and she was on Schitt's Creek

00:04:33.044 --> 00:04:35.124
- [Kelly] I love Schitt's Creek.

00:04:35.124 --> 00:04:36.040
- [Demi] I just think she's so beautiful

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.273
and so funny and timing is great.

00:04:38.273 --> 00:04:39.270
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.960
- [Demi] And then she
was on my podcast and

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.453
she brought it up and I was like, "no!"

00:04:42.453 --> 00:04:45.210
but it was okay, god I mean look at that.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.116
- I know, she's so cool, she's so funny.

00:04:46.116 --> 00:04:49.943
I love that show so much on
my god I was so sad it's over.

